From d3f84420738ffb67821cff6d103b0ccfaf5acaf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: justinh20 <justin.hanke@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:21:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/23] fix(tui): send the configured tier from TUI/desktop
 builds, and audit what was asked
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

_make_agent passed service_tier= to AIAgent but never request_overrides=,
and transports emit the tier only from the overrides — so a tier set in
config.yaml was parsed, stored, reported in session info, and dropped on
the wire for every TUI/desktop session (priority on main today, not just
flex). The bridge resolves the effective tier once (session pin > config),
gated to static tiers on the current route, and merges it over the
resolved entry's request body per #127015's two-dict contract. The typed
/fast mirror now keeps request_overrides in lock-step (off clears the
pinned keys; on re-resolves per provider so a mismatched
service_tier/speed pair is unrepresentable). turn_finalizer's billing
audit reads the top-level tier shape the transports actually send, not
only the custom-provider extra_body nesting — documented as a
request-side reading.

Fixes #101513.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
